    <!-- Add at least 3 examples -->

    <example xml:id="PRECALC-ATdgOiokWi" original="PRECALC/modules/m49455/index.cnxml" license="CC-BY-4.0">
      <title>Finding the Derivative of a Polynomial Function</title>
      <statement>
        <p>Find the derivative of the function <m>f(x)=x^{2}-3x+5</m> at <m>x=a.</m>
        </p>
      </statement>
      <solution>
        <p>We have:</p>
        <p>
          <md>
            <mrow>f'(a)=\lim_{h \to 0}\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h} &amp; \text{ Definition of a derivative }</mrow>
          </md>
        </p>
        <p>Substitute <m>f(a+h)=(a+h)^{2}-3(a+h)+5</m> and <m>f(a)=a^{2}-3a+5.</m>
        </p>
        <p>
          <md>
            <mrow>f'(a)=\lim_{h \to 0}\frac{(a+h)(a+h)-3(a+h)+5-(a^{2}-3a+5)}{h}</mrow>
            <mrow>=\lim_{h \to 0}\frac{a^{2}+2ah+h^{2}-3a-3h+5-a^{2}+3a-5}{h} &amp; \text{ Evaluate to remove parentheses }.</mrow>
            <mrow>=\lim_{h \to 0}\frac{\cancel{a^{2}}+2ah+h^{2}\cancel{-3a}-3h\cancel{+5}\cancel{-a^{2}}\cancel{+3a}\cancel{-5}}{h} &amp; \text{ Simplify }.</mrow>
            <mrow>=\lim_{h \to 0}\frac{2ah+h^{2}-3h}{h}</mrow>
            <mrow>=\lim_{h \to 0}\frac{\cancel{h}(2a+h-3)}{\cancel{h}} &amp; \text{ Factor out an }h.</mrow>
            <mrow>=2a+0-3 &amp; \text{ Evaluate the limit }.</mrow>
            <mrow>=2a-3</mrow>
          </md>
        </p>
      </solution>
    </example>

